G2610.def:
κατ-αγωνίζομαι depon., "perfective" compound (M, Pr., 116); 
__1. to struggle against. 
__2. to conquer, overcome: Hébreux 11:33.†

G2634.def:
κατα-κυριεύω 
[in LXX: Genèse 1:28 (כָּבַשׁ), Psaumes 110:2 Sir.17:4, al. ;] 
to gain or exercise dominion (over); 
__(a) absol. (Arist.); 
__(b) with genitive (Arist., al.): Matthieu 20:25, Marc 10:42, Actes 19:16, 1 Pierre 5:3.†
SYN.: (κατεξουσιάζω) (see Swete, Mk., l.with)

G2675.def:
κατ-αρτίζω 
[in LXX chiefly in Ps (Psaumes 8:2 al.; כּוּן, etc.) and Ezra (כְּלַל) ;] 
to render ἄρτιος, i.e. fit, complete; 
__(a) to mend, repair: Matthieu 4:21, Marc 1:19; 
__(b) to furnish completely, complete, equip, prepare: pass., Luc 6:40, Romains 9:22, Hébreux 11:3; mid., Matthieu 21:16 (LXX), Hébreux 10:5 (LXX); 
__(with) in ethical sense, to prepare, complete, perfect: Galates 6:1 (EV, restore), 1 Pierre 5:10; pass., 1 Corinthiens 1:10 (Field, Notes, 167), 2 Corinthiens 13:11, Hébreux 13:21 (cf. προ-καταρτίζω).†
